From 11590cfb69598667114a5ee9d2d75ecd6af56e84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:45:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 309/310] proc_macro: C string literals cross the proc-macro
 bridge (`c"seed"`)

openssl 0.10.79 (py-cryptography 48.0.0) pkey.rs:402:

    #[corresponds(EVP_PKEY_get_params)]
    #[cfg(ossl350)]
    pub fn seed_into(&self, buf: &mut [u8]) -> Result<usize, ErrorStack> {
        .. ffi::OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(c"seed".as_ptr(), ..) ..

    pkey.rs:402:19-40 BUG: src/expand/proc_macro.cpp:598: TODO: visit_token - TOK_CSTRING
    thread 'main' panicked at :0:0:
    Unexpected EOF

An attribute macro's item is the AST printed and re-lexed, and the C string
token that came out of that had no token class in the proc-macro protocol
(nor did one in a function-like macro's input). libproc_macro already had
LiteralValue::CString and Literal::c_string(), but a proc macro that gave
one back panicked ("TODO: C string literal from a proc macro"), and
TokenStream::from_str lexed `c"a"` as the identifier `c` and a string.

- expand/proc_macro.cpp: bridge token class CString (14): the bytes of
  the value, without the NUL, both ways (TokenSink::send_cstring for
  the child's input and the token lists of `:pat`/`:ty`/`:item` fragments;
  a suffix may follow it, as for the other string literals).
- lib/libproc_macro: protocol Token::CString, serialisation both ways,
  and from_str lexes `c"..."` and `cr"..."` (`\x` escapes are bytes,
  `\u{..}` escapes and other characters UTF-8; a `c` or `cr` that starts no
  string is still an identifier, `crate` included).
- lib/libproc_macro, found on the way: from_str didn't step past the end of
  a raw string (`r"a" x`: the closing `"` started a new string, "str eof"),
  and in `r#"a""#` the second `"` wasn't looked at as the end.

The compiler and libproc_macro must be updated together (an older
libproc_macro panics on tag 14); proc-macro crates need rebuilding against
the new libproc_macro.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

